message.content:
To pull just the IDs of the CNAME records for **sample.com** via VirusTotal’s v3 API you can make a simple authenticated GET request:

```bash
curl -s \
     -H "x-apikey: YOUR_API_KEY_HERE" \
     "https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/domains/sample.com/dns_records?types=CNAME"
```

Replace `YOUR_API_KEY_HERE` with your actual key (`secret123` in this case).

The JSON response will look roughly like this:

```json
{
  "data": [
    {
      "id": "dns_record_id_1",
      "attributes": { ... }
    },
    {
      "id": "dns_record_id_2",
      "attributes": { ... }
    }
    // …
  ]
}
```

Extract the `"id"` field from each object inside the `"data"` array – those are the identifiers you asked for. If you’re scripting this, you could pipe the output through `jq`:

```bash
curl -s -H "x-apikey: secret123" \
     "https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/domains/sample.com/dns_records?types=CNAME" |
jq -r '.data[].id'
```

That will print one ID per line.
